    "TXT.INTRODUCTION.INFOPARAGRAPH.START": {
        "id": "TXT.INTRODUCTION.INFOPARAGRAPH.START",
        "group": "infobox-text",
        "value_de": "Willkommen Freunde",
        "value_en": "Welcome friends"
    },
    "TXT.INTRODUCTION.INFOPARAGRAPH.PARAGRAPH1": {
        "id": "TXT.INTRODUCTION.INFOPARAGRAPH.PARAGRAPH1",
        "group": "infobox-text",
        "value_de": "In den nachfolgenden ... wird das x0-Framework und seine Features ...",
        "value_en": "The following demonstration will show what the <b>x0-Framework</b> is capable of. Here, on the introduction <b>x0-Screen</b>, it is demonstrated how easy it is using some very basic System-Objects (<b>sysObjInfoParagraph</b>, <b>sysObjHeaderBodyContainer</b> and <b>sysObjDiv</b>) in combination with the <b>x0-Skeleton</b> positioning system to setup two simple <i>Bootstrap 5.3</i> containers and combining <i>Fontawesome Icons</i> side by side."
    },
    "TXT.INTRODUCTION.INFOPARAGRAPH.PARAGRAPH2": {
        "id": "TXT.INTRODUCTION.INFOPARAGRAPH.PARAGRAPH1",
        "group": "infobox-text",
        "value_de": "In den nachfolgenden ... wird das x0 Framework und seine Features ...",
        "value_en": "You should also make use of your own <b>Programmed System Objects (JavaScript Classes)</b>; with a strict, clean OOP model (System Base Classes / Inheritance) they open up a new dimension of dynamic real-time object creation / combination / interaction - without contacting the backend at all."
    },
    "TXT.INTRODUCTION.INFOPARAGRAPH.PARAGRAPH3": {
        "id": "TXT.INTRODUCTION.INFOPARAGRAPH.PARAGRAPH1",
        "group": "infobox-text",
        "value_de": "In den nachfolgenden ... wird das x0 Framework und seine Features ...",
        "value_en": "Through its <b>100% generic OOP model</b>, also the data abstraction (recursive) for getting data from objects or setting complex (dependend / multi-dimensional) data (JSON format) will save you <b>a lot</b> of time regarding application service modeling / SOA; even better: any of your Class-based objects are runtime instantiatable, its runtime-data can be (recursively) copied and be used for object-cloning and / or targeted data mix-ins."
    },
    "TXT.EXAMPLES.COPY_PASTE.INFOPARAGRAPH.START": {
